# Self-service golden turns (obviously FICTIONAL), INCLUDING ADVERSARIAL out-of-scope asks.
#
# `expected_outcome` is what a compliance reviewer says the gate should have done, written from
# the allowlist pack rather than from a run. `expected_handoff` is the trigger they would expect.
# The adversarial rows are the reason gate precision must be 1.0: a gate that is right about the
# easy rows and wrong about these is worse than no gate, because it is trusted.
#
# Fields: id, contact_id, market, locale, text, requested_action, parameters, expected_outcome,
# expected_handoff, expected_executed, adversarial.
